# NOTHING THAT COULD CARRY DATA. The image is the tool; an
# extract or a run directory swept into a layer would travel
# with every pull of it, which is the worst possible way for a
# record to leave an account.
# RECURSIVE, BECAUSE A TOP-LEVEL PATTERN IS NOT A PROTECTION.
#
# These read `data/`, `*.csv`, `run_*/` and were matched against
# the path relative to the context ROOT only - so a csv anywhere
# below the top level sailed through, and
# docs/e2e/generated_patients.csv was found INSIDE the built
# image. The stated protection is that an extract swept into a
# layer would travel with every pull, and it did not hold for
# any file in a subdirectory. Found by looking in the image
# rather than by reading this file.
#
# Both forms are kept: some Docker versions do not match a
# root-level file with `**/`.
data/
**/data/
*.csv
**/*.csv
*.parquet
*.xlsx
# RUN DIRECTORIES STAY ROOT-ONLY, AND THE RECURSIVE FORM IS A
# TRAP. Docker cleans a trailing slash off a pattern, so
# `**/run_*/` becomes `**/run_*` and matches
# `scripts/run_all_smokes.py` and `scripts/run_discovery.py` -
# it silently removed the net and the runner from the image, and
# the documented "prove the tool works" command then failed with
# "No such file or directory". Caught by running the net inside
# the image; no text check could have seen it.
#
# Root-only is also sufficient: the record-bearing content of a
# run directory is its csv, and `**/*.csv` above catches that at
# any depth.
run_*/
.venv*/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# AND NOTHING THAT THE TEAM BUNDLE ALREADY REFUSES TO SHIP.
#
# `make_team_bundle.py` keeps an EXCLUDE_FILES list for the
# filtered export: the lab notebook, the sprint board, the
# runbooks that carry a machine's real paths, the demo scripts and
# the personal scanner that contains the patterns it scans for.
# An image that may run in a hospital's own AWS account is a
# second way out of this repo, and it had no such list at all.
#
# THIS DUPLICATES THAT LIST, WHICH THAT FILE ALREADY CALLS A KNOWN
# RISK - "if this list changes, that file must change with it".
# There are now three copies (bundle, operator export, here). A
# single source of truth would be better and is named as owed.
RUNBOX.md
RUNBOX.html
CONVENTIONS.md
docs/SPRINT.md
docs/WINDOWS.md
docs/DEMO_LLM_WINDOWS.md
docs/demo_script.md
docs/demo_script_v2.md
docs/demo_script_clinic.md
docs/demo_prompt.md
# An internal working note addressed to a named colleague. Fine
# in the repo and fine in the team bundle, which goes to people in
# this organisation; not something to ship in an image that may
# run in an account outside it.
docs/RAI_EVIDENCE_INDEX.md
